<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109015" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποπτήσσω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>crouch</i> or <i>cower beneath,</i>
			like hares, birds, etc., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πετάλοις ὑποπεπτηῶτες</span> (
				Ep.
			
			pf.
			part. from shorter stem <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτη-,</span> cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατα-,
			προσ-πτήσσω</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.312
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποπτήξας τάφῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					1203
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέπτηχε</span>”
				<i>cowers,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Musc.Enc.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>crouch before</i> another, <i>bow down to,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.5.1
			</span></i>; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. τοὺς νέους θεούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					960
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.6.8
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τῶν Ἀθηναίων ἀξίωμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					2.105
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i>to be modest</i> or <i>shy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.3.8
			</span></i>.</div>
